From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:29:04 -0800
Subject: [Media] Fix UrlData::CanAcceptDataFrom CHECK failures

Fix two cases where UrlData::CanAcceptDataFrom() returned true before
UrlData::SetDataOrigin() and false immediately afterward, tripping the
post-TryInsert() / post-RedirectTo() CHECK in
ResourceMultiBufferDataProvider::DidReceiveResponse():

1. A pre-response CrossOriginFail() sets is_cors_cross_origin_ = true
   while data_origin_ remains unset. Check is_cors_cross_origin_
   mismatch whenever data_origin_.has_value() || is_cors_cross_origin_
   before returning early on !data_origin_. Also avoid synthesizing a
   null KURL() in MergeFrom() when other->data_origin_ is unset.
2. In CORS_UNSPECIFIED mode, compare *data_origin_ != origin directly
   before calling SecurityOrigin::AreSameOrigin(), so identical URLs
   whose origins serialize as fresh random opaque nonces (such as
   revoked blob:null/... URLs in sandboxed iframes or data: URLs) always
   match themselves.

Bug: 579225207
Change-Id: I076ed3712a904317d8e6eeefc8dfcf5280b9eddb
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8684371
Auto-Submit: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Ted (Chromium) Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ted (Chromium) Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
